Implement file loading IO for local files on a hard drive. It should support exact addresses, and allow users to load an audio in the editor, in which case that audio file becomes a shader constant added to the prelude. 
When loaded, an enum entry in the prelude will be added so that the user can address the audio as a constant. These will be addressed as Clips::enum_name and returns a WaviateAudio object.
The editor will include a list view that can open to the side of the code editor on the right. This will let you add new file references or delete cached audio files.
If you ever call loadAudio from within the shader, this UI will update and add a new audio clip reference. when an audio is cached, it will show up as 1 a URL (read only if gotten from the shader. otherwise it will be a open file button and becomes read only once a file is selected), 2 a textbox to name It
if its not loaded from the shader but manually loaded via the open file button. If loaded from the shader this box won't even be visible. Next to that will be a trash bin icon to remove the loaded audio clip from the cache.
finally there will be a button at the bottom to totally clear the cache of all audio clips, and right above that, a memory indicator that shows the total mbs currently loaded of audio.
